      "notes": "Pactbound is an adult dark-fantasy game for players 18 and over. It\r\ncontains:\r\n\r\nSacrifice, grief and moral compromise. The core mechanic is bargaining\r\naway your memories, your years and the people you love. That is the\r\npoint of the game, not a side effect.\r\n\r\nImplied sensuality and gothic decadence. Brothels exist. Romance can be\r\npolyamorous and can be queer. Nudity appears in painted art, never as\r\nthe focus. There is no explicit sex. There are no minors in any sexual\r\nor romantic context, ever.\r\n\r\nBlood, violence, body horror and ritual imagery, painted rather than\r\nphotographic, but not softened.\r\n\r\nVillain paths, betrayal and broken oaths. The game records what you did\r\nand does not forget it.\r\n\r\nThemes of memory loss, mourning and harm accepted as the price of a\r\nbargain. These are implied and felt rather than shown directly."
